# The per-target re-inclusion stress: highway compiles the *same header* several
# times within one translation unit, once per SIMD target, by #including it
# again under a different HWY_NAMESPACE (foreach_target.h). One spelling of a
# member therefore has many expansions that need not agree, which is exactly
# the shape the macro-body veto exists for -- at a scale nothing else in the
# corpus reaches. It is also the only repo here built with target-specific
# copts on nearly every target, so it exercises the aspect's copts plumbing.
REPO_KIND=git
REPO_URL=https://github.com/google/highway.git
REPO_REV=2607d3b5b0113992fe84d3848859eae13b3b52c1   # 1.4.0
TARGET_PATTERN='//...'
RUN_TESTS=0
